imp72 (0.9.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * The compiler is IMP all the way down but the seed: the runtime library is
    IMP and imp72 builds it for any target (tools/mkrt.sh), the code generator
    is LLVM in the compiler's own process, and the programs are linked by lld
    in that process, so the package needs the C library's development files
    and no C compiler.
  * The seed (imp72stage0) no longer emulates the 36 bit PDP-10: it reads the
    64 bit syntax and its code generator is a C port of the compiler's own.
  * Runs on Linux, macOS, FreeBSD, OpenBSD, NetBSD, and amd64, i386, arm64,
    armv7, riscv64, ppc64le, s390x and loong64.

 -- David Walther <tederific@gmail.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 07:39:05 -0700

imp72 (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * First packaging: the stage 0 compiler (a C port of the kernel of
    Bilofsky's IMP72), the original syntax file, the translator to pcc IR, the
    pcc code generator on amd64, the C back end elsewhere, and the runtime.

 -- David Walther <tederific@gmail.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:23:12 -0700
